    },
    "Supports physiological functions through various mechanisms including enzyme cofactor activity, antioxidant effects, neurotransmitter precursor supply, hormonal modulation, or direct receptor interactions. Mechanisms vary widely and are substance-specific." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "通过多种机制支持生理功能，包括酶辅因子活性、抗氧化效应、神经递质前体供应、激素调节或直接的受体相互作用。机制差异很大，且具有物质特异性。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "透過多種機制支持生理功能，包括酶輔因子活性、抗氧化效應、神經傳導物質前體供應、激素調節或直接的受體相互作用。機制差異很大，且具有物質特異性。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Swallowed THC passes through your liver first, which turns much of it into 11-hydroxy-THC — an active by-product that reaches the brain more easily and binds the CB1 receptor far more strongly than THC itself. That's why an edible tends to feel stronger, milligram for milligram, than the same amount smoked." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "口服的 THC 会先经过肝脏，其中大部分被转化为 11-羟基-THC——一种活性代谢物，它更容易进入大脑，并且与 CB1 受体的结合远比 THC 本身更强。这就是为什么按毫克计算，食用大麻通常比吸食同等剂量感觉更强。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "口服的 THC 會先經過肝臟，其中大部分被轉化為 11-羥基-THC——一種活性代謝物，它更容易進入大腦，並且與 CB1 受體的結合遠比 THC 本身更強。這就是為什麼按毫克計算，食用大麻通常比吸食同等劑量感覺更強。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "swift-collections and swift-async-algorithms. Copyright © Apple Inc. and the Swift project authors." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
